  "inputs": [
   {
    "text": "Right — the coursebook. Peter, you had the strongest view last time, so start us off.",
    "voice_id": "BIvP0GN1cAtSRTxNHnWS",
    "speaker": 0
   },
   {
    "text": "My view has not changed. Unit seven is too long for the hours we have. Eighteen hours, twenty on paper, and either way the writing gets cut. I would drop the second reading text and give that time back to the writing.",
    "voice_id": "sfJopaWaOtauCD3HKX6Q",
    "speaker": 1
   },
   {
    "text": "I would keep the second text. It is the only place where they read two sources against each other, and that is the thing they actually cannot do yet.",
    "voice_id": "Ha9f2JUQ4LL1bw2ZcNjS",
    "speaker": 2
   }
  ],
